{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevGc6opWSpFjWD6MRBpm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt:46-52` - getById uses ResourceNotFoundException for missing shipments\n- `ShipmentController.kt:27-33` - create uses ConflictException for duplicate shipments\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` - ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException exist, mapped to 409 and 404\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` - ErrorCode enum defines machine-readable codes (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:42-84` - Tests follow MockMvc pattern, assert both status and error envelope structure\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Errors thrown by controllers are caught by GlobalExceptionHandler and rendered as ApiError envelope\n- ConflictException → 409 Conflict with error code\n- ResourceNotFoundException → 404 Not Found with error code\n- Tests assert `$.error.code` and `$.error.message` in error responses (not just status code)\n- POST endpoints that create resources return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(saved)` with 201\n- Endpoints that retrieve/transition return just the object (Spring defaults to 200 OK)\n- Error codes use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE and are part of the public API contract\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Must add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` error code (the enum is the authoritative list of API error codes; I cannot avoid this)\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Must add `confirm` endpoint at POST `/{shipmentId}/confirm` (the new feature itself)\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Must add tests to verify all 4 cases work and persist correctly (acceptance criteria require tests)\n\n**Risks:**\n- If I misspell or misuse the error codes, tests that check `$.error.code` will fail\n- If confirm returns wrong HTTP status (should return 200 OK for state transition, not 201), it violates REST conventions\n- If idempotency is not implemented correctly, acceptance criterion about retry succeeding could fail\n- If I use Shipment data class incorrectly, the immutability pattern might cause unexpected behavior\n\n**Open questions:**\n- None—the requirement is fully specified. CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED (idempotent), CANCELLED→409, not found→404.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum (line after SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS) to represent a shipment that cannot be confirmed because it is already cancelled.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new endpoint `POST /{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Calls `repository.findById(shipmentId)` to load the shipment\n   - If null, throws `ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)`\n   - If status is CREATED, calls `repository.save(shipment.copy(status = ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED))` and returns it\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws `ConflictException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_CANCELLED, ...)`\n   - Returns just the Shipment object (Spring will serialize as 200 OK)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add 4 new test methods:\n   - `test_confirms_a_created_shipment()` - creates S-1 with status CREATED, confirms it, verifies 200 OK and status is now CONFIRMED\n   - `test_confirm_is_idempotent()` - creates S-2, confirms twice, second confirm also returns 200 OK with status still CONFIRMED\n   - `test_confirm_rejects_a_cancelled_shipment()` - creates S-3, manually sets it to CANCELLED in repository, tries to confirm, expects 409 Conflict with error code SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\n   - `test_confirm_returns_404_for_unknown_shipment()` - tries to confirm S-missing, expects 404 Not Found with error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative approaches considered and rejected:**\n- Create a ShipmentService layer: Rejected because the existing code has no service layer (see OrderController); this would add a new architectural pattern and violate \"preserve existing architecture\"\n- Return 201 Created from confirm: Rejected because 201 is for resource creation; confirming a shipment transitions state on an existing resource, so 200 OK is correct per REST conventions\n- Throw an exception for already-confirmed: Rejected because the requirement explicitly states \"succeeds and changes nothing\" for idempotency (needed for retry safety)\n- Use a different error code like INVALID_SHIPMENT_STATE: Rejected because it's less specific; SHIPMENT_CANCELLED describes the actual reason for rejection\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case 1: Confirm CREATED shipment (success, 200 OK)*\n- Client: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (empty body)\n- Controller: repository.findById(\"S-1\") → Shipment(..., status=CREATED)\n- Controller: repository.save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED))\n- Repository: updates store[\"S-1\"] to Shipment(..., status=CONFIRMED)\n- Response: 200 OK, body = Shipment(..., status=CONFIRMED)\n\n*Case 2: Confirm CONFIRMED shipment (idempotent, 200 OK)*\n- Client: POST /shipments/S-2/confirm\n- Controller: repository.findById(\"S-2\") → Shipment(..., status=CONFIRMED)\n- Controller: returns shipment unchanged (no save call)\n- Response: 200 OK, body = Shipment(..., status=CONFIRMED)\n\n*Case 3: Confirm CANCELLED shipment (error, 409 Conflict)*\n- Client: POST /shipments/S-3/confirm\n- Controller: repository.findById(\"S-3\") → Shipment(..., status=CANCELLED)\n- Controller: throws ConflictException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_CANCELLED, \"...\")\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: catches exception, returns 409 with ApiError envelope\n- Response: 409 Conflict, body = { \"error\": { \"code\": \"SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }\n\n*Case 4: Confirm non-existent shipment (error, 404 Not Found)*\n- Client: POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm\n- Controller: repository.findById(\"S-missing\") → null\n- Controller: throws ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, \"...\")\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: catches exception, returns 404 with ApiError envelope\n- Response: 404 Not Found, body = { \"error\": { \"code\": \"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1 (`test_confirms_a_created_shipment`): Covers acceptance criteria #3 (confirm works and persists), #4 (error responses consistent)\n- Test 2 (`test_confirm_is_idempotent`): Covers acceptance criteria #5 (repeated confirm succeeds), #4 (consistent responses)\n- Test 3 (`test_confirm_rejects_a_cancelled_shipment`): Covers acceptance criteria #5 (cancelled shipment refused with proper error), #4 (consistent error envelope)\n- Test 4 (`test_confirm_returns_404_for_unknown_shipment`): Covers acceptance criteria #5 (unknown id refused), #4 (consistent error envelope)\n\nAll tests use MockMvc.perform() with status() and jsonPath() matchers to verify HTTP status and response body structure, matching the existing test convention.\n\n---\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3078,"cache_read_input_tokens":19024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3078},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"032f42af-434d-4517-b4e6-fab8c482f287","uuid":"e6b3bb49-1254-4159-9e27-7a2122e4f43d","timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:57:29.048Z","request_id":"req_011CevGc6K49DeDsim4Ea589"}
