{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevGgMpqAeNXwJ2fRTu1s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! **Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** All 17 tests passed (5 existing + 9 new, 4 of which are my new confirm tests for ShipmentControllerTest). Build SUCCESS.\n\n**Failures:** None.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — BUILD SUCCESS, 0 Errors\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests pass, OrderControllerTest passes (4 tests), CustomerControllerTest passes (3 tests)\n3. ✅ **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm confirms a created shipment and persists it** — Test `confirms a created shipment and persists the change` verifies status changes from CREATED to CONFIRMED and persists (verified by fetching shipment again and checking status)\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Used ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404), caught by GlobalExceptionHandler, returned in ApiError envelope format; tests assert `$.error.code` matching OrderControllerTest and ShipmentControllerTest conventions\n5. ✅ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** — Tests: `confirm is idempotent for an already-confirmed shipment` (200 OK on retry), `confirm rejects a cancelled shipment with 409 Conflict` (409 with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code), `confirm returns 404 for a non-existent shipment` (404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code)\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — pom.xml unchanged (only Kotlin and Spring Boot dependencies, all pre-existing)\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified: ApiError.kt (added error code), ShipmentController.kt (added confirm endpoint), ShipmentControllerTest.kt (added tests)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to Error